I'm reviewing AI security architecture patterns written by Mandiant (e.g., On-Behalf-Of (OBO) token delegation pattern; Securing the Agent Development Lifecycle on Amazon Bedrock AgentCore with Okta). Goal: NOT to create new patterns, but to identify missing security controls and assess risk coverage, then give recommendations. Use plain, simple language. For every finding: (1) what the risk is, (2) why it is a risk, (3) which control is missing.

METHOD
1. Risk coverage: use OWASP risks as rows; cite MITRE ATLAS techniques as evidence.
2. Control gaps: map each risk to controls via the OWASP Crosswalk, primarily CSA AICM (and NIST 800-53 if relevant); check whether the pattern implements each control.
3. Pattern-specific deep check: OAuth/IETF specs for OBO; AWS SRA/AgentCore guidance for AWS patterns.

OUTPUT TABLE
| Risk (OWASP ID) | ATLAS technique | What the pattern says | Status (Covered / Partial / Gap / Not addressed) | Missing control (AICM / RFC / AWS ref) | Recommendation |

